Sackar Atlas is a public data project by Anna Roberts.

It uses AI tools to synthesise data from public records — the [Special Commission of Inquiry into LGBTIQ hate crimes report](https://www.nsw.gov.au/departments-and-agencies/cabinet-office/resources/special-commissions-of-inquiry/lgbtiq-hate-crimes), [police data](https://data.nsw.gov.au/data/dataset/?tags=Police+Department) — with information from press archives ([Trove](https://trove.nla.gov.au/)) and [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Main_Page). The aim is to make the connections between cases, locations, institutions, and people visible in a way a 3,000-page PDF cannot.

The site is designed for community organisations, journalists, researchers, and the general public to use freely. [Source code on GitHub](https://github.com/bitsloppy/sackar-atlas)
